Send the review agent's request_render tool non-strict; its schema is unchanged.

On 2026-11-13 a paid scene-configuration run stopped in ARTISAN's review phase
(P5_review) when the OpenAI Responses API refused a request with HTTP 400
invalid_function_parameters: "Invalid schema for function 'request_render': At
schema path /properties/pose/type/0, object schema must define properties".
The review tool's `pose` is a free-form joint name -> value map
({"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": "number"}}). The codec sends
every tool except read_file with "strict": true, and strict function calling
cannot express a map. The API had accepted the same schema earlier in the same
phase and in earlier runs; it now refuses it.

The tool definition declares itself non-strict and the codec honours that, as it
already does for read_file. Nothing the model sees changes except the strict
flag: the description, the parameters and the codec's normalisation (every
property listed as required, optional ones nullable) are byte-identical, so the
prompts that write `pose={joint: value}` stay true. The coding agent's
request_render (no `pose`) stays strict. Other providers' converters read only
tool["function"] and ignore the new key.

Without strict mode the API no longer guarantees the argument shape, and
`_request_render` converted its arguments before its own `try`, so a malformed
call (a null or text pose value, a pose sent as a list or a string, views or
focus that are not lists of strings, arguments that are not an object) raised
out of the tool loop and ended the run. It now checks the shape first and answers
a malformed call with one ERROR sentence naming the expected shape; a well-formed
call is handled exactly as before. read_file, non-strict upstream, raised the same
way on a path that is not a string or arguments that are not an object, in both
the coding and the review harness; it now answers those with an ERROR too.

Applied after 0002-gpt-6-1-sol.patch, against
physicalvision/Artisan@ad322b5b31e50bdb84155520f09622c00c6056c3.

